    ordenada = sorted(lista)
    resultado = []
    for x in ordenada:
        if x in resultado:
            resultado.append(x)
    return resultado[:3]

Hey, help me optimize this PHP snippet. It's supposed to check for duplicate entries in an array, but it seems super inefficient on big arrays. Can you rewrite it cleaner and faster? The current code is: 

function findDuplicates(array $array) {
    $counts = [];
    foreach ($array as $item) {
        $counts[$item] = ($counts[$item] ?? 0) + 1;
    }
    $duplicates = [];
    foreach ($counts as $key => $value) {
        if ($value > 1) {
            $duplicates[] = $key;
        }
    }
    return $duplicates;
}

